# Crates allowed to fail to build in the Linux release job.
#
# The Linux CLI release builds each crate independently. A crate that does not
# build fails the release — and therefore blocks `publish` — unless it is named
# here. Listing one is a deliberate, reviewable decision to ship a Linux tarball
# that does not contain that tool; the release notes say so in a banner and the
# job is annotated as degraded.
#
# Format: one crate name per line; `#` starts a comment. Put the reason in a
# comment above the name, and remove the entry once the build is fixed — the
# gate warns about entries whose crate builds fine.
#
# Empty on purpose: as of v0.1.3 all four CLI crates build on Linux and the
# shipped tarball contains all five binaries.
